</span></span><span class=3D"highlight-line"><span class=3D"highlight-line-=
content">
</span></span><span class=3D"highlight-line"><span class=3D"highlight-line-=
content">I have used **HTML5 Canvas** for the graphics and **JavaScript** f=
or the physics (gravity, collision detection, and scoring). No external ima=
ges or downloads are required; the game draws the bird and pipes using code=
.<!-- -->
</span></span><span class=3D"highlight-line"><span class=3D"highlight-line-=
content">
</span></span><span class=3D"highlight-line"><span class=3D"highlight-line-=
content">### How to run this:<!-- -->
</span></span><span class=3D"highlight-line"><span class=3D"highlight-line-=
content">1.  Copy the code block below.<!-- -->
</span></span><span class=3D"highlight-line"><span class=3D"highlight-line-=
content">2.  Create a new file on your computer named `game.html`.<!-- -->
</span></span><span class=3D"highlight-line"><span class=3D"highlight-line-=
content">3.  Paste the code into that file and save it.<!-- -->
</span></span><span class=3D"highlight-line"><span class=3D"highlight-line-=
content">4.  Double-click `game.html` to open it in your web browser.<!-- -=
->
</span></span><span class=3D"highlight-line"><span class=3D"highlight-line-=
content">
</span></span><span class=3D"highlight-line"><span class=3D"highlight-line-=
content">```html<!-- -->
</span></span><span class=3D"highlight-line"><span class=3D"highlight-line-=
content">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;<!-- -->
